      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hoplias_cf_teres_en/",
      "html": "<p>This trahira was imported from Venezuela for the first time, and only very few specimens arrived. H. teres was described by Valenciennes in 1847 from Lake Maracaibo in Venezuela.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hoplias_cf_teres_en/",
      "html": "<p>The new species differs from all Hoplias imported so far by its brilliantly coloured eye. However, the scientific name H. teres, a species described by Valenciennes in 1847 from Lake Maracaibo in Venezuela, cannot be confirmed for certain. The specimens were 14-18 cm long at the time of import.</p>"
    }
